    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2525B\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the insurance law, in relation to\nannuity dividend reinvestment\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo provide for the election of automatic reinvestment of dividend\ndistributions.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend paragraph (6) of subsection (b) of\nsection 4231 of the Insurance Law to reference for purposes of an\nindividual participating annuity contract, the clarification\napplicable to participating income annuity contracts set forth in new\nparagraph (8) of subsection (b) of section 4231 of the Insurance Law\nthat the annuitant may elect to reinvest the annuity dividend.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would amend paragraph (7) of subsection (b) of\nsection 4231 of the Insurance Law to reference for purposes of a group\nparticipating annuity contract, the clarification applicable to\nparticipating income annuity contracts set forth in new paragraph (8)\nof subsection (b) of section 4231 of the Insurance Law that the\nannuitant may elect to reinvest the annuity dividend.\n\nSection 3 of the bill would amend section 4231 of the Insurance Law to\ncreate a new paragraph (8) of subsection (b) to clarify that for\npurposes of individual or group participating income annuity\ncontracts, the annuitant may elect to reinvest the annuity dividend.\n\nSection 4 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis proposal seeks to amend § 4231 of the insurance law to clarify\nthat paid-up additions are an option for the use of policyholder\ndividends by annuitants. This revision is beneficial to the annuity\ncustomer since it will allow them to have the option to automatically\nreinvest their policyholder dividend distributions to paid-up\nadditions in their annuity contract, which can then be converted into\nfuture income.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
